    "created_at": "2016-06-02T21:20:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-02T21:20:21Z",
    "body": "In a quick code review over IM @annevk said\n\n> I'd prefer a wrapper for the exception throwing\n> \n> Having to continue reading after an exception is thrown seems very unnatural\n\nI'm not quite sure what that means. My intention with those was to parallel the common programming construct `try { ... } finally { ... }`. If you have suggestions on better ways to make that clear I'd appreciate it.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
